@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
+= Zig I/O lexical guard
+
+This gate scans tracked and non-ignored untracked Zig source throughout the
+repository, including modules imported by an FFI. It is not an effect-system
+proof and does not resolve import aliases or external library effects.
+
+Direct `std.fs`, `std.io`, and `std.Io` accesses are rejected except for the
+exact, memory-only `fixedBufferStream(...)` call. Allowing that call does not
+allow other I/O on the same line, namespace aliases, or similarly named APIs.
+Comments and string literals are not interpreted as executable source.
+Ordinary Zig compilation remains necessary; malformed source is not validated
+by this lexical check.
+
+This keeps the old repository-wide safety horizon while repairing the false
+positive for stateful-artefacts' pure domain serializer (issue #42). No
+whole-file or whole-namespace exclusion is introduced.
+
+Run `bash actions/zig-unified-api-adapter-check/test.sh`. The test is wired into
+the independent Composite shell contract CI job, so a broken transitive action
+pin cannot prevent the positive and negative controls from executing.
